Andrew Gabriel (Andrew@cucumber.demon.co.uk) wrote:
: I'm looking at the DLPI interface on DEC Alpha OSF/1 V2.0 as a means
: of accessing LLC1 over Ethernet. There is a man page for dlpi/dlb
: indicating the DEC implementation is a "Style 2" implementation, which
: requires the use of DL_ATTACH_REQ to identify the Physical Point of
: Attachment (PPA), i.e. which hardware interface on the machine you
: wish to access.

: This PPA identification is passed as a value on the DL_ATTACH_REQ,
: and is system/manufacturer dependent. I want to access the Ethernet
: port on the back of the machine, but nowhere can I find what value
: I should give in the DL_ATTACH_REQ for this (or any other) interface
: in DEC's implementation.

: Does anyone know how DEC map hardware interfaces to PPA values?
It's documented in the Network Programmer's Guide, section 2.5 on DLPI,
including an example program with the Streams ioctl required to identify
the PPAs. I've incorporated this code into applications and can verify
that it works.

