I posted follow ups to two different articles but my Agent newsreader
(very cool system) doesn't seem to like it when you do a follow up
article. So this is a repost and a test to see if a new post is
working ok with Agent.

Don't use INN with advfs on your news partition. I went through the
exact same hell where I had lots of disk space and tons of inodes. But
I would get "No space on Device" and INNWATCH would lock the puppy up
on me.  I could not make any files manually on that partition after
taht point either.

The solutino was to wipe that partition and set it up as ufs. I talked
to DEC but they are not sure what to do about it. I am sure it is a
bitch of a problem to find.

I have been having lags on my machine as well. I have a DecAlpha with
128 megs of ram and the load average is only around 1. In talking to a
very smart Dec person, he seems to think it is a good chance that 128
meg is not enough ram OR some major tweaking has to be done. He sees
that a huge amount of CPU time is being used for "system" activities
so there is not too much of the CPU left for regular processes.

Kinda sucks doesn't it?

DANO




