Actually, the name is Digital UNIX. It seems in a brand identification
review, the market did not associate DEC with Digital Equipment Corp.
so DEC is out. Expect name changes in future products and upgrades to
reflect this trend.

As far as the Open prefix goes, this could happen but is unlikely. UNIX
is an open op/sys to begin with, so Open Digital UNIX would be somewhat
redundant. We suspect marketing is trying to stress that Digital is in
the UNIX arena and still provide our brand identity.

