|> but it works.

You probably haven't seen a german lk401 keyboard yet. It's quite
impossible to do ctrl-[ there ;)

What _always_ works in DEC world is ctrl-3  (i.e. ctrl and the digit
key 3). ctrl just zeros out bits 5-7, leaving a control character.
Bits 0-4 of [ and 3 are identical. This works for ctrl-/ and ctrl-]
as well (with 4 and 5), ctrl-/ is used for the quit signal in Unix,
and ctrl-] makes sense with telnet and kermit.

On X11 I usually hardcode F11 to send Escape via xmodmap. Try f.i.:

xmodmap -e 'keysym F11 = Escape"

