TIB citation/reference making package used in conjunction with the
TeX typesetting package.  More particularly, their experience in
running the package on an Alpha under OSF/1.  I have had difficulty
in getting it to function correctly.  The package (including the
current version) has been around since 1989 and functions perfectly
on other machines, particularly those operating under other versions
of Unix.  Is there something odd with the OSF/1 environment or am I
doing something wrong?  Any assistance would be gratefully received.

I asked the substance of this question on comp.text.tex but was not
overcome by replies.  Maybe the question was put to the wrong newsgroup.

Here is the story.

I have down-loaded a copy of the TIB program suite from CTAN and I am
having difficulty in getting it to behave correctly.  There appears to
be one, if not more, bugs in the programs.  I am using a DEC Alpha
workstation operating under OSF/1 3.0.

I followed the directions contained in the INSTALL file relating to
the  tib.h  file.  The BBBBB entries were changed to the absolute path
of the directory into which all the TIB files had been loaded.  The
CCCCC entry was changed to the absolute path to the  common  file and
the FFFFF was likewise set to the absolute path to the  INDEX  file.

What is not explained in the documentation is the use of  %D  format
specifications in the  tibdex.c  file.  These need converting to  %d
entries.  BUG 1.

Make was then applied, resulting in the 4 executables.

A  test  subdirectory was created and the  test.tex  and  test.ref
files were copied into it.  The command:
    tibdex test
in accordance with the documentation was given.  The result was a  INDEX
file which was identical to the one included in the TIB suite.  The
command:
    tib test
again in accord with the documentation, was given.  On the display was
produced:
    Tib -- version 2.2, released 12/15/89.
    Processing format commands ...
    Reading input document file test.tex and looking up references ...
