    locate: first key (dieck) matched too many refs
    'test.tex', line 22: multiple references match dieck
    .
    .
    .
    locate: first key (peitge) matched too many refs
    'test.tex', line 39: multiple references match peitgen
    Processing citations ...
    Writing output file ...
    Output of tib in test-t.tex.
The file  test-t.tex  was put through TeX and the resulting  dvi file
was viewed.  The citations contained in the text appeared as [1], [1,1],
[1,1,1], and [1,1,1,1].  The reference list consisted of the one entry --
[1].

The warning messages from  tib  appear to be of some substance, despite
being annoying.  The resulting article is less than impressive
particularly as it is the demonstration provided with the package.
The documentation says that the [] escape sequence in the  tibbed
article would produce a reference list tabulation -- it did not.  By
contrast, the command:
    tiblist test.ref
produced a file that generated a perfectly good reference listing once
passed through TeX.

There is either a bug in the code of  tib  or I have it setup
incorrectly!  Somebody else must have experienced the same problem, and
and found a solution.

Ross
