Thomas Leitner (tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at) wrote:
: 1.) Most fonts appear much bigger on the screen than they used to on the
:     my old DecStation 5000/33 running Ultrix 4.4. I got the same display
:     resolution of 1280x1024 and the same font specification results
:     in a much bigger font. How can I change that? I installed all fonts
:     offered by the OSF/1 installation program.

The font path for the X server under Digital Unix (the operating
system formerly known as DEC OSF/1) has the 100dpi fonts before the
75dpi fonts (this is all from recollection, they may in fact only have
the 100dpi fonts in their path by default).  The default setup under
Ultrix is to only use 75dpi fonts.

You can fix it by starting up your x server with a different font
path. Check the file /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers.  You will see a
program specified there called /usr/bin/X11/X.  This is a symbolic
link to Xdec.  The man page for Xdec specifies switches you can use to
change the font path. Make these changes in the Xservers file.

I personally like using 100dpi fonts since it gives me a wider range of
options for font sizing.

