si_value is defined as _sifields._sigproc._sigrt._sigval in siginfo.h
and this seems to create a problem.  I noticed that si_value was not
defined in pre-3.2 versions of OSF/1, so I just put an #undef si_value
in mhn.c and it seemed to take care of things.  Unfortunately I am not
a C programer, so I have no idea what I actually changed, but mhn
seems to work properly.

I also get an undefined symbol of _putchar when linking xvmh, but
nobody here uses xvmh, so I didn't bother to try and fix it.

