Watch out for the metacell limit. Apparently, though there's no problem with
inodes in AdvFS, there's a problem with a limit on number of metacells, and
they appear to be used up as files are deleted and recreated. The 3.2
release notes supposedly contain a note about this, and you can add a -x
parameter to the mkfdmn command that creates the file domain. That
parameter, sadly, is only available on 3.2.

