I have run the same programs, using identical source code, on identical
Alphas, under both OSF/1 and AXP/VMS (using the same hardware, in fact).
Performance is very close as expected for both systems. If I had to make
any observations concerning performance differences, it would be that
code in which floating-point operations are not predominant tends to
run faster under OSF/1 than VMS, while code in which floating-point
operations do predominate tends to run faster under VMS than OSF/1.
For my code, at least.

