>the SPECfp92 for the SS20/HS11.  You generally do not use SPECfp92 
>for multi-CPU machines like the 20/612.

Generally people don't because they don't have automatic multi-threading
compilers.  The SS20-612 was run with a multi-threading FORTRAN compiler
which produced significant speedups when compared to a uni-processor.
Since there were no source code changes there is the possibility that
certain "real" codes will also see a speedup on the MP systems.  Your
mileage may vary.

Facts:
