In article <3ks9m2$cfp@sundog.tiac.net>,
David L. Nye <evil@max.tiac.net> wrote:
>DEC 3000/600 Alpha OSF/1 3.x 
>
>Anyone have one of the new Seagate Baracuda 4.2 GIG, ST15150N?
>
>How about a disklabel incantation to set up a 3gig and a 1 gig 
>partition on it? :)

Try running  disklabel -rw /dev/rrz#c ST15150N, where # is the number
of the drive.

If ST15150N isn't a valid entry in /etc/disktab, then it should query
the drive about its geometry & so forth.  Then you run disklabel -e on
it & set up the partitions however you like.


