and them rm'ing hundreds of thousands of files. In OSF 3.2, there's a
mkfset switch to do this.

More to the point, I find it relatively outrageous that there's no
definitive way to determine how much room is left on an AdvFS volume.
I had a long, unfruitful discussion with Digital support on this issue,
the sum of which is that none of the tools df, showfdmn showfsets are
completely accurate. But this is no more outrageous than the fact that
a vdump/vrestore of a fileset silently deletes all quota information.

It's less outrageous than the number of AdvFS file system inconsistency
panics we see, but I'll give Digital a day or two more to fix that
before I post that flame...

