    If it's a JetDirect II card (the current flavor), lpd works as well as
telnet streaming. The only trick is that there are two queues, text and
raw, the latter for PostScipt if your LaserJet supports it.

    Here are our printcap entries for an HP 4SiMX are:

lp1|1|soho-laser2|HP LaserJet 4 SiMX (remote):\
        :lf=/usr/spool/hp4simx/errors:\
        :lp=:\
        :mx#0:\
        :rm=<printer-IP-address>:\
        :rp=text:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/hp4simx:

lp2|2|soho-post2|HP LaserJet 4 SiMX PostScript queue (remote):\
        :lf=/usr/spool/hp4simx/errors:\
        :lp=:\
        :mx#0:\
        :rm=<printer-IP-address>:\
        :rp=raw:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/hp4simx:

