BE CARE !! the 3rd step says: 
  3. Create a file in the /var/spool/pop directory called POP 

  but it's not correct, the dir. might be
                           /var/spool/pop/pop actually the home 
directory of pop account (owned by pop) !!


My troubles were coming reading the man pages.
This version of POPD uses a private databases /var/for users instead of use 
/etc/passwd unlike other version of popd from the net; this can be and 
advantage to subscribe a user only for mail purpose w/out giving him/her 
a real account.
The other face of the coin is the password handling that might be done by
the superuser or "pop" account.

