How can a POP subsciber change by itself his/her own password ? 

Eudora hypercard stack refer to unix programs that comunicate on port
106/tcp with the password change command in Eudora, but they use the
system passwd command to change a user password, but a POP subcriber may
not be a real user, so no entries in /etc/passwd will be found !!

Great ! may be changing the code and using popwrd instead of passwd should 
work. Has anyone working on it ???

