That's only one of the causes, and it will report the client's hostname.
In general the "not responding" messages come from a overloaded Ethernet,
and given that any alpha box can saturate an ethernet, even with NFS,
I'd guess that's where the problem lies.

Are you talking through routers?  (The "traceroute" command can help
check that.)  If so, many routers drop more messages than they should
between busy subnets, and that may be the main problem.  If so, you
can sometimes do better by mounting with a smaller wsize or rsize value
(they default to 8192 bytes), but performance may decline.

