In article <3k556e$92i@uplherc.upl.com>, SKJ <skj@upl.com> writes:
> I looking for information from anyone that has installed an HP 
> JetDirect card in an HP Laserjet and then setup OSF1 to print to it.
> HP has just told me that it is impossible, but I would think that someone
> has probably done it.  Please inform me of anyone that may have created
> a JetDirect driver for OSF1.  Where can I get it? How does it Work?

Since HP and DEC are competitors I have little hope either of them
will ever acknowledge it will work.

Depending on the exact JetDirect card, you have a couple of choices.

Any JetDirect card talking TCP/IP can accept a print file on port 9100.
You'll need a filter program in your printcap entry to pipe the output
to port 9100 on the printer.  There are several free ones available on
the net.

Later (?modern?) JetDirect cards support the lpd protocol.  Setup your
printcap for a remote lpd using the printer's IP number.  This is much
easier, and I would recommend getting the JetDirect card which supports
it.
