Dave,

This is very simple.  Just have CNAME records in DNS for your "aliases" that
point to your "real" host.

We have a server that provides, gopher, ftp, http, and a few other services 
and the server has a name for each type of service: gopher.xxx.com,
ftp.xxx.com, www.xxx.com, etc.

Enjoy!

