>"it cannot load the file into shared memory"
>The file is about 10 MB  in size. The program works with smaller files.

The default maximum size of shared memory is 4 MB (in OSF/1 2.x). 

>Can I change the "size of shared memory"?
>If so, what are the kernal parameters that control it and where do I enter them 
>in the configuration file?

In OSF/1 2.x you use the 'shmmax   xxxx' parameter in the kernel
configuration file, and then rebuild the kernel. I put it immediately
before the 'config vmunix' line, but it shouldn't sensitive for
position.


