ge Armhold) writes:
:|:
:|:The "-i" option for performing interactive restores using vrestore
:|:seems to be broken under 3.0B:
:|:
:|:: magnus:4]/backup/foo#vrestore -i -f - < dump.out
:|:: vrestore: Date of the vdump save-set: Sun Mar  5 17:29:21 1995
:|:: (/) 
:|:: (/) unknown command
:|:
:|:It just scrolls on and on with  "(/) unknown command".  Does anyone
:|:know if there is a workaround for this, or if it has been fixed in
:|:3.2?  Non-interactive restores work just fine.


:Uhhh, how do you expect to do an interactive restore if you are redirecting
:input from a file??? You CAN'T do that...unless the program opens a separate
:input channel to the terminal, which vrestore doesn't appear to do...

Because it *should* re-open the input terminal.  This works just fine
for regular dump & restore:


: tenebris:3]/backup/foo#restore -i -f - < ../dump.out
: restore : ls
: .:
:  .Xauthority        .xsession-errors   etc/               tmp_mnt/
:  .rhosts            backup/            slocal/
:  .rhosts~           dev/               tmp/
: 
: restore > 

My reason for redirecting input rather than opening the file
explicitly is because we run dump/restore via a rather complicated
Perl program that dumps & restores via a rsh stream. i.e. rather than
reading from a tape device we're reading from a rsh data pipe.

vrestore is just as broken when opening the file explicitly (vrestore
-i -f filename).

-George
