Everhard Faas (faas@apd.dec.com) wrote:
: I have an axp 3000/500. I like to add 2 turbo channel ethernet
: controllers to the system, to make a multi-homed host.The PMAD 
: network cards are installed in turbo channel slot 3 and 4.
: I think that I have to change the /usr/sys/conf/<NODE> file...
: The original line in that file for the ethernet controllers is:

: controller      ln0        at tc0       slot  7 vector    lnintr

: I think I have to add the next 2 lines:

: controller      ln1        at tc3       slot  ? vector    lnintr
: controller      ln2        at tc4       slot  ? vector    lnintr

: But I don't know what I should use for the slot number... And I don't
: know what lnintr means.

Hi.
In your /sys/conf/NODE file, you have to add :
controller      ln1        at tc0       slot  3 vector    lnintr
controller      ln2        at tc0       slot  4 vector    lnintr
because you've just add cards, not TC. lnintr is the interruption handler.
Gilles.


