Rob> Anyone any idea what I'm doing wrong?

Yes.  You're trying to use a setuid shell script.  DEC OSF/1
closed the inherent security hole with them by refusing to honour
setuid bits on scripts.

If you really need something like this to work, you need to use a
wrapper program to do the job.  However, most wrapper setups for
this just re-introduce the original problem, so be careful.
There are pointers to additional information on wrappers for
scripts in the comp.lang.perl meta-FAQ (indirectly, anyway, via
the full FAQ).

