Whils a CNAME would work for this, they require an extra lookup each time (this
is a recursive lookup internal to the DNS and pretty much invisible to the
user, but it does take machine cycles and, depending on the configuration of
the zones, network bandwidth) and are processed by BIND very differently form
most queries. Whenever possible (and there are some cases when it is not), I
strongly recommend use of additional A records.

That all said, if you don't control the zones for aaaa.com, bbbb.com, cccc.com,
and DDDD.net, you may be in a situation where a CNAME is the only answer.

