>Hi,

Hello Stranger.

>Can I change the "size of shared memory"?

>If so, what are the kernal parameters that control it and where do I enter them 
>in the configuration file?

There are four kernel options you can set in your system configuration file.
They are:

option	Usage			      [Default Value]

shmmin	Min. shared mem. segment size [1]
shmmax 	Max. shared mem. segment size [4194304]
shmmni	Num. of shared mem identifiers [100]
shmseg	Max. num. of attached shared mem. segments/process [32]

In the config file, you could increase shmmax like so:

shmmax 8388608

And this would give you an 8 meg max segment. Pax.

-- 
