In article <1995Mar2.012836.44543@yogi.urz.unibas.ch>, 
rosenth@foto.chemie.unibas.ch (Lukas Rosenthaler) writes:

>I consider buying a AlphaStation 400/233 with the ZLX-E3 graphics board.
>Since I will use the machine for both NT and OSF/1 (with dual boot
>disks), I'll need to know if the drivers for the ZLX-E3 is on the
>standard distribution of OSF/1 (on CD) ? The reason for this question is
>that there are different part number for ordering the ZLX-E3 for NT
>versus OSF/1. Therefore I think to get the NT version and buy a
>licence/media kit for OSF/1 (which I need anyhow). But it's not clear if
>the ZLX-drivers are included (The licence *WILL* include OPEN3D!).

The separate part number for NT is due to the drivers being included on a
separate floppy that comes with the board.  Digital pays a license for
each of the NT-style boards with driver, whereas for OpenVMS and OSF/1
the license cost (and the driver) is folded into the operating system.

If you buy a license/media kit for OSF/1 (including Open3D) it will have
the proper drivers.

