    In the code below, if memp is the pointer returned by malloc,
    then size is the number of bytes.

    #define ALIGNSIZE sizeof (double)

    typedef struct MEMPTR { 
      unsigned size;
      unsigned filler;
      unsigned data [ALIGNSIZE];
    } memptr;


