An mfs filesystem is pageable. In fact it is created inside the virtual
space of a special process, and is in no way fixed in memory.
If you are short on RAM, this process (and the pseudo-RAMdisk) can be
paged and even swapped, so can finally end up on your disk into the swap
space.
