In article <3it7ad$pac@delphi.bc.edu>, lauri@bcuxs1.bc.edu (Lauri S. Doniger) writes:
|> 
|> I was wondering if anyone has set up OSF/1 systems within a cluster, and
|> if they provide load sharing as well as failover capability as do the VMS clusters.  
|> 
|> Thanks for any input!


what we call our 'cluster' (7 machines) is simply NIS(YP) and NFS.
By NFS-mounting the /usr partition we make sure that all machines
behave the same way. the 'satellites' can use their local disks
for a large (256MB) swap-file and local (fast) disk-storage.

We use only one NFS- and NIS server cause it's more stable
than cross-mounted disks.

We have very stable operation for one year now!

There's no load sharing, and what is 'failover capability' ?


